                        <idno>Conti Rossini 66</idno>
                    </msIdentifier>
                    <msContents>
                        <summary>Protective Prayers</summary>
                        <msItem xml:id="ms_i1">
                            <title type="incomplete" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT6845PPSatolay">Prayer against the pain caused by Tǝgrǝtyā, Šotalāy and Šotalāyt</title>
                            <note>In comparison to the attestation in <ref type="mss" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/ANLcr32#ms_i1">Rome, Biblioteca dell’Accademia Nazionale dei Lincei, Conti Rossini 32: Protective prayer against šatolāy, with ʾasmāt (in ms_i1)</ref>, the incipit in this scroll is 
                                shorter and directed not only against Šotalāy and Šotalāyt, but also against Tǝgrǝtyā.</note>
                            <textLang mainLang="gez"/>                            
                            <incipit xml:lang="gez">በስመ፡ <gap reason="ellipsis"/> ጸሎት፡ በእንተ፡ ሕማመ፡ ትግርትያ፡ ወሾተላይ፡ ወሾተላይት፡ ዘትቀትል፡ ሕፃናተ፡
                                እምሐልኩከ፡ ወአውገዝኩከ፡ ወአሰርኩከ፡ ወለጐምኩከ፡ ከመ፡ ኢትቅትል፡ ሕፃናተ፡ ኃተምኩከ፡ በማኅተመ፡ አብ፡ ወወልድ፡ ወመንፈስ፡ ቅዱስ፡ ፩ አምላክ፡ 
                                አሰርኩከ፡ አንተ፡ ሾተላይ፡ ወሾተላይት፡ በዝንተ፡ አስማት፡ መአጁን፡ መአጁን፡ ፈቃጁ፡ መጂር፡</incipit>
                        </msItem>
                        <msItem xml:id="ms_i2">
                            <title ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT7601PPSalomon">Protective prayer for the excommunication of šetolāy and
        šetolāwit by the names of the five nails of the cross</title>
                            <note>In comparison to the attestation in <ref type="mss" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/ANLcr32#ms_i2">Rome, Biblioteca dell’Accademia Nazionale dei Lincei, Conti Rossini 32: Protective prayer for the excommunication of šetolāy and
        šetolāwit by the names of the five nails of the cross (in ms_i2)</ref>, the incipit in this scroll is 
                                shorter and the name of Šotalāyt was omitted.</note>
                            <textLang mainLang="gez"/>                            
                            <incipit xml:lang="gez">ሰሎሞን፡ ሎፍሐም፡ ንምሎስ፡ ዮፍታሔ፡ <gap reason="ellipsis"/> አምሐልኩከ፡ <gap reason="ellipsis"/> 
                                አንተ፡ ጋኔን፡ ሾተላይ፡ ከመ፡ <supplied reason="lost">ኢትቅርቡ፡</supplied> ኀበ፡ ነፍሳ፡ ወሥጋሃ፡ ለዓመትከ፡ <gap reason="lost"/>
                                    </incipit>
                        </msItem>
                        <msItem xml:id="ms_i3">
                            <title ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT6609ProtectPrayer">Prayer against pains caused by Zār, Tǝgrǝtyā, Bāryā and Legewon, Dask and Gudāle</title>
                            <note>The incipit contains <term key="MagicSymbols" ana="#MagicSymbols">magic glyphs (charaktêres)</term>. Similar to 
                                <ref type="mss" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/ANLcr32#ms_i3">Rome, Biblioteca dell’Accademia Nazionale dei Lincei, Conti Rossini 32: Protective prayer against various illnesses and demons (in ms_i3)</ref>, this prayer is also directed against Zār, Bāryā, Dask, Legewon and Gudāle,
                                but it also targets Tǝgrǝtyā.</note>
                            <textLang mainLang="gez"/>                            
                            <incipit xml:lang="gez">በስመ፡ <gap reason="ellipsis"/> አድኅና፡ እምሕማመ፡ ዛር፡ ወትግርትያ፡ ባርያ፡ ወሌጌዎን፡ ደስክ፡ ወጕዳሌ፡ ወኵሉ፡ ደዌ፡
                                ለአመትከ፡ <gap reason="lost"/></incipit>
                        </msItem>
                        <msItem xml:id="ms_i4">
                            <title ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT7872Tegretya">Prayer against Tǝgrǝtyā</title>
                            <textLang mainLang="gez"/>                            
                            <incipit xml:lang="gez">ትግርትያ፡ ተሰደዱ፡ በሰሀለል፡ ትግርትያ፡ ተአሰሩ፡ ሎኤ፡ ሎኤ፡ ሎኤ፡</incipit>
                        </msItem>
                        <msItem xml:id="ms_i5">
                            <title ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT4622Prayer">Ṣalot baʾǝnta ḥǝmāma qʷǝrṭat</title>
                            <textLang mainLang="gez"/>                            
                            <incipit xml:lang="gez">ቁርፀት፡ ዘተፈተወት፡ እምኀበ፡ አብ፡ ወወልድ፡ ወመንፈስ፡ ቅዱስ፡ ከመ፡ ይርዳእ፡ ወይቤዙ፡ ለውሉደ፡ እጓለ፡ እመሕያው፡ እንዘ፡ 
                                ይበጸብጽ፡ ከርሠ፡ ወይጐጸንጕጽ፡ ገበዋተ፡ ወይጠዊ፡ አንጀተ፡ ወቈነጥን፡ አማዑተ፡ ሽገር፡ ሽገር፡ ሽገር፡ ሽገር፡ ሽገር፡ ሽገር፡ ሽገር፡</incipit>
                        </msItem>
                        <msItem xml:id="ms_i6">
                            <title ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT4705MagicPr">Ṣalot baʾǝnta ḥǝmāma wǝgʿāt</title>
                            <textLang mainLang="gez"/>                            
                            <incipit xml:lang="gez">ጸሎት፡ በእንተ፡ <surplus>በእንተ፡</surplus> ሕማመ፡ ውግዓት፡ አላህ፡ መላህ፡ በላህ፡</incipit>
                        </msItem>
                        <msItem xml:id="ms_i7">
                            <title ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT4620Prayer">Ṣalot baʾǝnta ḥǝmāma nahabt wa-ʾagānǝnt ʾAlāhumā Wayānurā</title>
                            <note>In contrast to its attestation in <ref type="mss" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/BAVet77">Vatican City, Biblioteca Apostolica Vaticana, Aeth. 77</ref>, the text of this scroll is directed only against
                                blacksmiths, but not against demons (<foreign xml:lang="gez">ʾagānǝnt</foreign>).</note>
                            <textLang mainLang="gez"/>                            
                            <incipit xml:lang="gez">ጸሎት፡ በእንተ፡ ሕማመ፡ ነሃብት፡ አላሁማ፡ ወያኑራ፡</incipit>
                        </msItem>
                        <msItem xml:id="ms_i8">
                            <title ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT7873Spirits">Ba-zǝntu ʾasmātika yǝtḥarad</title>
                            <textLang mainLang="gez"/>                            
                            <incipit xml:lang="gez">በስመ፡ <gap reason="ellipsis"/> አጁር፡ ናኤሆር፡ <gap reason="ellipsis"/> በዝንቱ፡ አስማቲከ፡ ይትኃረድ፡
                                ይትኃረድ፡ ይትኃረድ፡ <gap reason="ellipsis"/> ይቤሎ፡ አገዝኩ፡ ለዝ፡ ጋኔን፡ <gap reason="ellipsis"/> በዝ፡ ቃልከ፡ ተአሠሩ፡ መናፍስተ፡ ርኩሳን፡
                                ወሰብእ፡ መሠርያን፡ እምላእለ፡ አመትከ፡ <gap reason="lost"/></incipit>
                        </msItem>
                        <msItem xml:id="ms_i9">
                            <title ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT5135MagicFormula">Magic Formula Against Stomachache</title>
                            <note>The text in this scroll is entitled <foreign xml:lang="gez">Ṣalota ḥǝmāma karś</foreign> 
                                (‘Prayer against ache of the stomach’), while the text in another attestation in <ref type="mss" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/IVEf45">Saint Petersburg, Institut Vostočnyh Rukopisej Rossijskoj Akademii Nauk, IV Ef. 45</ref> is 
                                directed against <foreign xml:lang="gez">qʷǝrṣat</foreign>, which can also be interpreted as ‘stomach ache’ or ‘cramps’.
                                The end is missing.</note>
                            <textLang mainLang="gez"/>                            
                            <incipit xml:lang="gez">አልፍሉል፡ አልፍሉል፡ አልፍሉል፡ ጸሎተ፡ ሕማመ፡ ከርሥ፡ 
                                ዘይደ<supplied reason="omitted" resp="PRS8999Strelcyn">ነ</supplied>ጕዝ፡ ገበዋተ፡ ወይጠዊ፡ ወይሰብር፡ አንጀተ፡ ወአማዑተ፡
                                    </incipit>
                        </msItem>
                    </msContents>
